# Channels — main endpoints. Generated skeleton, synthetic data only.
# Path ids below are placeholders — replace with real ids from a list call.
@channelKey = telegram_business
@candidate = 1
# Variables: see rest/http-client.env.json (host, session, xsrf). How to get them: docs/guides/api.md
# Full list of Channels operations: /api/docs (tag "Channels").

### POST /api/webhooks/{channelKey} — channels.webhook
POST {{host}}/api/webhooks/{{channelKey}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/

### POST /api/webhooks/phonet — telephony webhook, token in a header (HRM-26). 200 when it matches the
### "Webhook token" field; wrong/missing → 401. Never put the token into the URL; placeholder only, the repo is public.
@phoneWebhookToken = YOUR_WEBHOOK_TOKEN
POST {{host}}/api/webhooks/phonet
Content-Type: application/json
X-Webhook-Token: {{phoneWebhookToken}}

{
    "event": "call.hangup",
    "uuid": "demo-call-1",
    "lgDirection": 4,
    "otherLegs": [{"num": "0500000000"}],
    "billSecs": 12
}

### POST /api/webhooks/ringostat — the same token as a Bearer value (also accepted: X-Signature = hex HMAC-SHA256 of the body)
POST {{host}}/api/webhooks/ringostat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{phoneWebhookToken}}

{
    "uniqueid": "demo-1",
    "call_type": "in",
    "caller": "+380500000000",
    "duration": 12
}

### POST /api/webhooks/binotel?token=… — DEPRECATED: 401 while the integration flag webhook_query_token is off (default);
### with the flag on (existing connections only) → 200 + "Deprecation" response header.
POST {{host}}/api/webhooks/binotel?token={{phoneWebhookToken}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

requestType=apiCallCompleted&callDetails[generalCallID]=demo-1&callDetails[callType]=0&callDetails[externalNumber]=0500000000

### GET /api/webhooks/{channelKey} — GET handshake (WhatsApp): echo hub.challenge as plain text
GET {{host}}/api/webhooks/{{channelKey}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

### GET /api/channels — GET /channels — which channels can send / call now (any active user)
GET {{host}}/api/channels
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

### POST /api/candidates/{candidate}/messages — channels.messages.send
POST {{host}}/api/candidates/{{candidate}}/messages
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "channel": "telegram",
    "text": "Example text"
}

### POST /api/candidates/{candidate}/call — channels.call
POST {{host}}/api/candidates/{{candidate}}/call
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/

### GET /api/channels/admin — channels.admin
GET {{host}}/api/channels/admin
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

